; Null-safe references (objfpc; item 2 of the proposals): the flow checks
; under {$nullsafe on}, declarations, and the switch.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/nullsafe/flow.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLOW
; FLOW: flow.pas:22:1: error: constructor 'CreateLazy' may leave field 'Boss' of the non-null type 'TCustomer' nil (assign it on every path, or declare it 'TCustomer?')
; FLOW: flow.pas:31:1: error: function 'Make' may return nil: its result of the non-null type 'TCustomer' may not be assigned (assign it on every path, or declare it 'TCustomer?')
; FLOW: flow.pas:29:10: warning: function 'Make' never assigns its result
; FLOW: flow.pas:36:5: error: function 'Pick' may return nil here: its result of the non-null type 'TCustomer' may not be assigned (assign it on every path, or declare it 'TCustomer?')
; FLOW: flow.pas:52:8: error: 'B' may be nil here, but 'A' is of the non-null type 'TCustomer'; check it first (if B <> nil then ...), or declare 'A' as 'TCustomer?'
; FLOW: flow.pas:55:11: error: 'B' may be nil here, but its member 'Name' is used; check it first (if B <> nil then ...), or use '?.Name'
; FLOW: flow.pas:56:7: error: 'B' may be nil here, but parameter 'c' is of the non-null type 'TCustomer'; check it first (if B <> nil then ...)
; FLOW: flow.pas:60:11: error: 'C' may not have been assigned yet (a reference of a non-null type must be assigned before it is used)
; FLOW: flow.pas:61:8: error: 'A' may not have been assigned yet (a reference of a non-null type must be assigned before it is used)
; FLOW: flow.pas:64:11: error: 'B' is nil here, but its member 'Name' is used
; FLOW: flow.pas:74:15: error: 'B' may be nil here: the loop may set it to nil before its next iteration; check it in the loop
; FLOW: flow.pas:77:8: error: 'B' may be nil here, but its members are used in 'with'; check it first (if B <> nil then ...)
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/nullsafe/decls.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DECLS
; DECLS: decls.pas:20:12: error: a nullable type cannot be given a name; write 'TSquare?' where it is used
; DECLS: decls.pas:21:20: error: '?' makes a class, interface or class-reference type nullable; 'integer' is not one
; DECLS: decls.pas:61:11: error: 's' may be nil here, but its member 'Area' is used; check it first (if s <> nil then ...), or use '?.Area'
; DECLS: decls.pas:63:8: error: 'c' is nil here, but its member 'Create' is used
; DECLS: decls.pas:64:8: error: nil cannot be used here: 't' is of the non-null type 'IShape' (declare 't' as 'IShape?' if it may be nil)
; DECLS: decls.pas:65:8: error: the result of 'Maybe' may be nil here, but 't' is of the non-null type 'IShape'; check it first in a local variable, or declare 't' as 'IShape?'
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/nullsafe/switch.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SWITCH
; SWITCH: switch.pas:2:1: warning: expected {$nullsafe on} or {$nullsafe off}; ignored
; RUN: %p3 --mode=tp -c %S/Inputs/nullsafe/tp.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TP
; TP: tp.pas:2:1: warning: {$nullsafe} needs --mode=objfpc; ignored
